  "APIProfile": "Basic",
  "Description": "MMC Multimodal Access Control (MAC) Module. Recognises a User from face and speech and issues a UserID plus a spoken/rendered verdict. Face Recognition and Speaker Recognition each read the User IDs (the enrolled gallery) and the Scene Descriptors from Shared Storage - these are NOT ports. Time (OSD-STM) accompanies each captured object and is supplied by the User Agent's clock. ID Reconciliation reconciles the two candidate Instance Identifiers; Response and Scene Rendering produces the Vocal Response and Face Descriptors. The User Agent drives this Module through the Controller (start, write boundary inputs, read boundary outputs); it never acts on the AIMs. The Controller runs the sub-AIMs and routes data among them by data type per this L3.",
